"""Full-size on-screen touch keyboard for Linux / KDE Plasma (Wayland/X11).

Features:
- Complete PC keyboard layout:
  * Full 4 Navigation Arrows (←, ↑, ↓, →), Home, End, PgUp, PgDn, Ins
  * Esc, Tab, Del, Backspace, Enter, Space, Caps Lock
  * Modifiers: Shift, Ctrl, Alt, Super (Meta/Win) with sticky/latched lock
  * Full Function keys (F1-F12), PrintScreen
  * Complete numbers and symbols row with Shift variants
  * Dedicated ?123 / Numpad layer and Fn layer with quick actions (Undo, Copy, Paste, etc.)
- Interactive Drag & Move (Header drag handle to float anywhere on screen)
- Dock / Float toggle (snaps to bottom or floats freely)
- Responsive Resize:
  * Size presets (S: 65%, M: 82%, L: 100%)
  * Scale / Zoom buttons (A-, A+)
  * Corner drag-resize grip (⤡)
- Auto-Pop on Text Field Tap & Auto-Minimize on Defocus (Dual AT-SPI & KWin Wayland integration)
- Minimizes to a floating pill (⌨) so it never gets in the way
- Injects keystrokes via Linux /dev/uinput (EV_KEY) - works across all applications
- Non-focusable window architecture: NEVER steals focus from target applications
"""
